      "note": "The searcher's text is escaped by connection.quote before it is interpolated. Entry.text_search_rank builds ts_rank(entries.tsvector_combined, ...) around the private Entry.tsquery_sql, which is the only way the query reaches SQL and which returns websearch_to_tsquery('english', <quoted literal>). Brakeman cannot follow through a private_class_method, so it flags the interpolation without seeing the quoting. Verified against the running database: Entry.search(%q{climate x'; DROP TABLE entries; --}).to_sql emits ...websearch_to_tsquery('english', 'climate x''; DROP TABLE entries; --')..., the embedded quote doubled and the payload confined to one string literal. A bind parameter is not available here: this expression is used as an ORDER BY term, where Rails does not bind, which is why the literal is quoted by hand. Restructuring was tried and rejected -- the only shape that quiets Brakeman inlines websearch_to_tsquery at each call site, duplicating the text search configuration that tsquery_sql exists to state once. If tsquery_sql ever stops routing the query through connection.quote, this ignore must go."
    },
